// §273 landing two — CZECH, the explainer. Keyed by the English source
// (normalized innerHTML for rich blocks, text for plate labels); see
// src/explain-i18n.js for why. Landing one (the chrome and the primer) left
// this surface out on purpose; this table declares it, so the row in
// src/i18n.js carries no `surfaces` field any more.
//
// Vocabulary is the SAME register tier one's chrome and the primer use
// (src/i18n.js, src/primer-i18n.cs.js), one name per part: strojek, švýcarský
// kotvový krok, krokové kolo, kotva (the pallet fork AND the alarm governor's
// anchor, the overload the review sheet asks about), nepokoj, vlásek, hnací
// pero, buben, fusée (the loan, indeclinable: kužel fusée, řetízek fusée),
// řetízek, pastorek, koruna, sloupkové kolo, regulátor budíku. The project's
// own words — the Vocabulary table's thirty — are coined once here and used
// everywhere: stanoviště, pásmo, vrstva / pruh, koridor, odstup (the one
// margin), azimut, mezikruží, tětiva, tečna, zdvih, obálka, jednotka, osa,
// poloha, řádek, brána, dolní mez / rozpočet, předání, výjimka, akční skupina,
// přímka, zalomení (a fold — never «překlad», which is a translation), odbočka
// (a fork), roh, vložené kolo, odvozený.
//
// Czech INFLECTS, and a quoted identifier does not: a case ending never rides
// inside the span, and the prose puts a noun in front of the token instead
// («v konstantě <code>CLEAR_MARGIN</code>», «sonda <code>probe-x.mjs</code>»)
// so the <code> gate stays byte-identical. The hidden .gloss-variants rows list
// the case forms the prose actually uses, read off this table's own text.
//
// NUMBERS AND <code> ARE NOT TRANSLATED — they are the source constants this
// page exists to quote, so 0.15 keeps its point here as in every locale, and
// the primer's 0,024 is the other page's rule, not this one's. Emphasis the
// English carries as CAPITALS rides the wording, never an added tag.
// «modelováno» vs «simulováno» tracks the repo's modelled/simulated
// distinction exactly; HONESTY.cs gates it (the participle stem modelov-,
// never the bare noun «model», which Czech also says for the credit line's AI
// model). The reader is addressed formally (vy).
//
// Drafted by machine, not reviewed by a native speaker: the terms a workshop
// may dispute are listed in tools/l10n-review/questions.mjs.
